# Copy to .env.local and fill in to enable real email login, cloud saves, and
# multiplayer rooms ("Play with friends" in Story).
#
# Without these, the game runs with a local dev fallback (email sign-in is faked,
# saves go to the browser's localStorage) and the friends panel shows a disabled
# notice. Solo play is identical either way. No code change needed to go live.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Create a free project at https://supabase.com
#   2. SQL editor → run supabase/schema.sql
#   3. Authentication → Providers → enable Email (magic link)
#   4. Authentication → URL Configuration → add http://localhost:3000 (and your prod URL)
#   5. Settings → API Keys → copy the Project URL and the publishable key
#
# NOTE ON THE KEY: Supabase replaced the legacy `anon` key with a publishable key
# (`sb_publishable_...`), and projects created since Nov 2025 have no anon key at
# all. The publishable key is a drop-in replacement — paste it below. The variable
# keeps its historical name; only the value's format changed. Never paste a
# `sb_secret_...` / service_role key here: NEXT_PUBLIC_* is shipped to browsers.
#
# NOTE FOR HOSTED DEPLOYS (Vercel etc.): NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined at BUILD
# time, not read at runtime. Adding or changing them in your host's dashboard does
# nothing until you trigger a fresh deploy.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
